WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.815 --> 00:00:02.413
- [Narrator] This is Sarita.

00:00:02.413 --> 00:00:04.855
She's a cotton-top tamarin,

00:00:04.855 --> 00:00:07.788
one of the smallest primates in the world.

00:00:07.788 --> 00:00:10.636
After years of being poached
and captured in the wild,

00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:12.393
the already endangered cotton-top

00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:16.310
now faces the rapid
destruction of its habitat.

00:00:21.223 --> 00:00:23.186
Cotton-tops are native to South America

00:00:23.186 --> 00:00:26.036
and can only be found in
a limited forested area

00:00:26.036 --> 00:00:28.072
of northwest Columbia.

00:00:28.072 --> 00:00:29.638
They makes their homes in trees there

00:00:29.638 --> 00:00:32.830
and enjoy a diet of fruits and insects.

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:34.950
Although exceedingly rare in the wild,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.852
cotton-tops are recognizable by the shock

00:00:36.852 --> 00:00:38.882
of white hair on their heads.

00:00:38.882 --> 00:00:41.162
These primates are social creatures.

00:00:41.162 --> 00:00:43.285
They live in hierarchical family groups,

00:00:43.285 --> 00:00:46.490
led by a dominant pair
of mating cotton-tops,

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.038
and the pair's offspring are raised

00:00:48.038 --> 00:00:49.819
communally by the group.

00:00:49.819 --> 00:00:51.578
For many years, their
numbers were decimated

00:00:51.578 --> 00:00:53.312
by the illegal pet trade

00:00:53.312 --> 00:00:55.908
and their capture for biomedical research,

00:00:55.908 --> 00:00:58.614
but today, deforestation
is the main culprit

00:00:58.614 --> 00:01:00.822
behind their dwindling numbers.

00:01:00.822 --> 00:01:03.593
Their wild population has shrunk by 80%

00:01:03.593 --> 00:01:06.065
over the past three generations.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:09.744
They're holding on by
the tips of their claws.

00:01:09.744 --> 00:01:12.327
This is the cotton-top tamarin.

